# One rounded sum. Not a kernel the library calls (its code is a + b): it states the bound of the
# center of a one-limb ball, from which ball_add_1 takes its constant unit_computed. Sharp in the
# form u/(1 + u), and exact in the subnormal range, where the sum of two numbers of the format is
# a number of the format.
kernel:        add_1_1
input:         a
input:         b
output:        s
value:         a+b
ensures:       rounded s nearest
ensures:       error s R c=1/(1+u) k=1 t=0
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/OneLimb.v add_1_1_correct
ieee_lead_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeFolds.v add_1_1_ieee_lead
ieee_bridge_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeMapSteps.v add_1_1_ieee_bridge
source:        one rounding to nearest, the bound u/(1+u) of JR18
license:       bound: published; proof: MIT
status:        proved
ieee:          bridge

s = add(a, b)
